robin <usenet@unrated.net> writes:

> It shouldn't be _too_ difficult to write a savelog file, prefereable in the
> same structure as the logfile, each time a player saves.  The Tournament could
> then list the most recent entry from that log for each player with either a
> saved game file or a game in progress lockfile.

Should be possible.. when a game is saved, call a modified copy of
the current topten function.
I think the copy should differ from the topten function in these points:
- use 1 as the PERSMAX value
- the ENTRYMAX shouldn't be used, so it will allow 
- search only matching player name instead of the player name & role
combination 
- of course, use a different file name..
- and the actual topten function should erase the entry from the save
record when it writes to the logfile

The function should also do all the score calculations that the done
function does, and be called AFTER the save file is written, to avoid
having to backtrack the side effects of the calculations.

